      "writtenOn": "2026-03-31T18:58:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "According to the comment you want this to swizzle from `(Cb, Y, Cr, 1)` to `(Y, Cb, Cr, 1)`, but if my matrix math is correct (and it may very well not be) this matrix would swizzle `(Cb, Y, Cr, 1)` -\u003e `(Y, Cr, Cb, 1)`? That would suggest that either the matrix of the comment is wrong?",
      "revId": "e80d684d89052d87420dbad62c01b7e63b5917d1",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "89e4c6ab_c129fb3a",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/ExternalTexture.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 62
      },
      "lineNbr": 202,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-01T14:42:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `yuvToRgbConversionMatrix` is multiplied on the right (see [1] and the comment in `ExternalTexture.h`), so what ends up happening in the shader is `rgb \u003d yuv * kUndoVulkanSwizzle * yMat` so the transpose of the matrix you\u0027d imagine being used is what\u0027s needed here.\n\nWhat\u0027s totally confusing (and confused me for another 20m when trying to answer this comment and figuring out how this works again) is that this is a column major matrix written with columns all on the same line. What you see in the source code is actually the transpose of the matrix.\n\nI\u0027ll file an issue to add a `Mat*::FromRows()` helper function that makes the matrix in the source look like what you\u0027d write on a piece of paper.",
      "parentUuid": "d3a7cfef_bbe6f3e0",
      "revId": "e80d684d89052d87420dbad62c01b7e63b5917d1",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
